{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Many days.</b> Three days (Sifra)." "<b>Outside the time of her menstrual impurity.</b> After the seven days of her menstrual impurity have gone out." "<b>Or if she has a flow.</b> These three days." "<b>Beyond her menstrual impurity.</b> Separate from her menstrual impurity by one day — this is a zavah, and her ruling is decided in this pericope, and not like the law of the niddah: this one requires counting seven clean days and a sacrifice, whereas the niddah does not require counting clean days, but seven days she remains in her menstrual impurity whether she sees or does not see. And they expounded in this pericope: eleven days between the end of one niddah and the beginning of the next niddah — any three consecutive days of flow she sees during those eleven days, she is a zavah."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:45.360935786Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}